  "type": "self",
  "prompt": "Let $a$ be a positive integer. Compute\n$$\\int\\left(\\tan^{a+3}(x)+\\tan^{a+2}(x)+\\tan^{a+1}(x)+\\tan^{a}(x)\\right)dx$$\nin terms of $a$. You do not need to include the $+C$ in your answer.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "$\\dfrac{\\tan^{a+2}(x)}{a+2}+\\dfrac{\\tan^{a+1}(x)}{a+1}$",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Factor with $\\sec^2$",
    "body": "Group: $\\tan^{a+3}+\\tan^{a+1}=\\tan^{a+1}(\\tan^2+1)=\\tan^{a+1}\\sec^2$ and $\\tan^{a+2}+\\tan^a=\\tan^a\\sec^2$. So the integrand is $\\sec^2x\\,(\\tan^{a+1}x+\\tan^ax)$. With $u=\\tan x$, $du=\\sec^2x\\,dx$, the integral is $\\int(u^{a+1}+u^a)\\,du=\\frac{u^{a+2}}{a+2}+\\frac{u^{a+1}}{a+1}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{\\tan^{a+2}x}{a+2}+\\frac{\\tan^{a+1}x}{a+1}$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "calculus",
   "trigonometry"
  ],
