  "type": "numeric",
  "prompt": "Compute the infinite sum\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{\\binom{n+1}{2}}=\\frac1{\\binom22}-\\frac1{\\binom32}+\\frac1{\\binom42}-\\frac1{\\binom52}+\\cdots.$$",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "4*ln(2)-2",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "answerDisplay": "$4\\ln2-2$",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Partial fractions",
    "body": "$\\binom{n+1}2=\\frac{n(n+1)}2$, so the sum is $2\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{n(n+1)}=2\\sum(-1)^{n-1}\\left(\\frac1n-\\frac1{n+1}\\right)$. Splitting, $\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}}n=\\ln2$ and $\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{(-1)^{n-1}}{n+1}=\\sum_{m\\ge2}\\frac{(-1)^{m}}{m}=1-\\ln2$. So the sum is $2\\left(\\ln2-(1-\\ln2)\\right)=4\\ln2-2$.\n\n**Answer: $4\\ln2-2$**"
   }
  ],
